# Flux-driven deposition, against the closed-form growth rate
#
# This is the whole chain with no free parameters.  For a Maxwellian at rest
# against a wall at the same temperature the impingement mass flux is
# rho*vbar/4, so a film that captures a fraction STICK of it and has bulk
# density RHOFILM must grow at
#
#   s = STICK * rho_gas * vbar / 4 / rho_film       vbar = sqrt(8kT/pi m)
#
# and value (21) reports what the surface actually did.  One number checks the
# new mflux_incident keyword, the area normalization, the sticking sum and the
# length/time conversion at once.
#
# The flux source consumes a mass FLOW -- norm flow, no area in it -- and
# divides by the cell's own total surface area itself.  That is not a detail:
# an implicit element takes the ID of the cell that made it, so a cell holding
# several elements has them all in one tally slot, and a compute normalizing
# by area would have divided each contribution by its own element's area and
# summed the results.  Summing the areas once, here, is the cell's flux.
#
# The surface is the same flat ramp in.test.flat uses, so the front is normal
# to x and the measurement needs no projection.

variable            STICK index 1.0
variable            NRHO index 1.0e20
variable            TEMP index 300.0
variable            RHOFILM index 2.0e3

seed                12345
dimension           2
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes

boundary            r r p

create_box          0 20 0 80 -0.5 0.5
create_grid         20 80 1
balance_grid        rcb cell

global              nrho ${NRHO} fnum 1.0e18

species             air.species N
mixture             air N temp ${TEMP} vstream 0.0 0.0 0.0

compute             FLUX isurf/grid all all mflux_incident norm flow
fix                 AVG ave/grid all 1 100 100 c_FLUX[*]
fix                 ablate ablate all 100 1.0 flux f_AVG &
                    density ${RHOFILM} sticking ${STICK} mode deposit

global              surfs implicit
read_isurf          all 20 80 1 ramp.20x80 127.5 ablate push no

surf_collide        1 diffuse ${TEMP} 1.0
surf_modify         all collide 1

create_particles    air n 0

timestep            1.0e-6

stats               200
stats_style         step np f_ablate f_ablate[21]

run                 1000
